+## Amendment — governing intent on every work item
+
+This amendment adds POC-REQ-014: every served work item carries a
+governing-intent field that is either an edge to its warrant, joined by a
+recorded identity, or Unknown with a reason from RFC2-24's closed list. Both
+channels count the Unknown items over the served set, and Trajectory marks
+them and lets a reader narrow the board to them, as RFC8-23 requires of work
+with no traceable warrant. No edge is ever derived from a title or other
+work-item text, so the non-goal above against inferred edges and intent
+stands unchanged.
+
+The amendment admits no new work-item column. Which input, if any, may carry
+a warrant into the POC is an open owner question, recorded as P-100 in
+`.syzygy/governance/decisions/PENDING-OWNER-DECISIONS.md`. Until it is
+answered, every served item is Unknown with the reason
+`source-uncaptured-or-unreachable`. In `CONTRACT-COVERAGE.md`, RFC8-22 and
+RFC8-23 move from Part B2 to Part A, because a requirement now covers one of
+their consequences, and the one limb no requirement observes has its own
+Unknown amendment row.
+
